<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hymn to the Nile</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The &quot;Hymn to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a>&quot;, also called the &quot;Hymn to Hapy&quot;, was created and sung by the ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egyptians">Egyptians</a> about the flooding of the Nile. The Greek historian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a> called <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> the &quot;Gift of the Nile&quot;, because ancient Egyptian civilization shaped its culture around the river and depended on its resources.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The &quot;<b>Hymn to the Nile</b>&quot;, also called the &quot;Hymn to Hapy&quot;, was created and sung by the ancient Egyptians about the flooding of the Nile.</blockquote><a href="/songs/hymn-to-the-nile">Hymn to the Nile</a></li></ul></section>
